<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodosius II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">401–450</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodosius II was emperor of the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> from 408 to 450, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadius">Arcadius</a> as a child. His reign saw the completion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walls-of-constantinople">Theodosian Walls</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, the founding of a school of higher learning in the capital and the Theodosian Code of 438, the first official collection of imperial laws. He paid large tributes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> and died after a riding accident.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodosius-ii.jpg" alt="Theodosius II" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Theodosius_II_Louvre_Ma1036.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
